          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Much has been said about
            %strong inverting a class of morphisms
            in a category (see
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            so it is locally small. One the other hand, we have
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+localization"} simplicial localization
            which retains all the homotopy information and returns an
            = succeed "-category." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            If we have a 2-category with a notion of weak equivalence, one could localize the underlying 1-category in a way hopefully compatible with the 2-arrows, or extend the result fully into the 2-dimensional setting. In general this will require bicategories, and is the subject of
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Pronk96"} Pronk 96
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
            with a class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            of 1-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"}> cells
            \.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            is said to
            %strong admit a right calculus of fractions
            if it satisfies the following conditions
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                [2CF1.]
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                contains all equivalences
            %li
              %p [2CF2.]
              %ul
                %li
                  a)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                  is closed under composition
                %li
                  b) If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\in W
                  and a iso-2-cell
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mover
                          %mo ⇒
                          %mo ∼
                        %mi b
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \stackrel{\sim}{\Rightarrow} b
                  then
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b\in W
            %li#2CF3
              %p
                [2CF3.] For all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi w
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                        %mo ′
                        %mo →
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w: A' \to A
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: C \to A
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w\in W
                there exists a 2-commutative square
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi P
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mi g
                            %mtd
                              %mi A
                              %mo ′
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi v
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⇒
                            %mtd
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mi w
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi C
                            %mtd
                              %munder
                                %mo →
                                %mi f
                            %mtd
                              %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\begin{matrix}
                      P&amp; \stackrel{g}{\to} &amp; A' \\
                      v \downarrow&amp;\Rightarrow &amp;\, \downarrow w\\
                      C &amp;\underset{f}{\to} &amp; A
                      \\end{matrix}
              %p
                with
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v\in W
            %li
              %p
                [2CF4.] If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo :
                      %mi w
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi f
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mi w
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha: w \circ f \Rightarrow w \circ g
                is a 2-cell and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w\in W
                there is a 1-cell
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in W
                and a 2-cell
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi β
                      %mo :
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi v
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mi g
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi v
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta: f\circ v \Rightarrow g \circ v
                such that
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi v
                        %mo =
                        %mi w
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi β
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha\circ v = w \circ \beta
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
                is an iso-2-cell, we require
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi β
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
                to be an isomorphism too; when
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v'
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi β
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta'
                form another such pair, there exist 1-cells
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi u
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi u
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u,\,u'
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi u
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v\circ u
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi u
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v'\circ u'
                are in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mo :
                      %mi v
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi u
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mi v
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi u
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon: v\circ u \Rightarrow v' \circ u'
                such that the following diagram commutes:
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi f
                              %mo ∘
                              %mi v
                              %mo ∘
                              %mi u
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo ⇒
                                %mrow
                                  %mi β
                                  %mo ∘
                                  %mi u
                            %mtd
                              %mi g
                              %mo ∘
                              %mi v
                              %mo ∘
                              %mi u
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi f
                              %mo ∘
                              %mi ϵ
                              %mo ⇓
                              %mo ≃
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ≃
                              %mo ⇓
                              %mi g
                              %mo ∘
                              %mi ϵ
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi f
                              %mo ∘
                              %mi v
                              %mo ′
                              %mo ∘
                              %mi u
                              %mo ′
                            %mtd
                              %munder
                                %mo ⇒
                                %mrow
                                  %mi β
                                  %mo ′
                                  %mo ∘
                                  %mi u
                                  %mo ′
                            %mtd
                              %mi g
                              %mo ∘
                              %mi v
                              %mo ′
                              %mo ∘
                              %mi u
                              %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\begin{matrix}
                      f \circ v \circ u &amp; \stackrel{\beta\circ u}{\Rightarrow} &amp; g\circ v \circ u \\
                      f\circ \epsilon \Downarrow \simeq &amp;&amp;
                      \\simeq \Downarrow g\circ \epsilon \\
                      \\\
                      f\circ v' \circ u' &amp;\underset{\beta'\circ u'}{\Rightarrow}&amp; g\circ v' \circ u'
                      \\end{matrix}
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is a category, then these axioms reduce to the ones of Gabriel and Zisman for a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calculus+of+fractions"} calculus of fractions
          %p
            Given such a setup, Pronk constructs the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            at
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            and the universal functor sending elements of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            to equivalences.
          %h2#example Example
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            be a category with binary products and pullbacks, together with a class of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/davidroberts/show/class+of+admissible+maps"} admissible maps
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem:
            %p
              The 2-categories
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat(S)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Gpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gpd(S)
              of categories and groupoids internal to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              admit
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory+of+fractions"} bicategories of fractions
              for the class of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/davidroberts/show/weak+equivalence"} equivalences
          %p
            The resulting localization is equivalent to the bicategory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anafunctor"} anafunctors
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Roberts12"} Roberts (2012)
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong (Grothendieck toposes as a bicategory of fractions of localic groupoids)
              %br/
            %p
              The category of etale-complete
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localic+groupoids"} localic groupoids
              (with open source and target maps) admits a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory+of+fractions"} bicategory of fractions
              at open essentially surjective fully faithful functors.
            %p
              The resulting bicategory is equivalent to the bicategory of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+toposes"} Grothendieck toposes
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphisms"} geometric morphisms
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphisms"} natural isomorphisms
            %p
              See Theorem 7.7 in
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Moerdijk"} Moerdijk
